| Keep reading | Ch. 37, lines 183–191, Keth asks to see what Cael has; Ch. 43, line 307, “I didn't send it. It went.” | **9/10, high.** The challenge, the watcher, Bede's counter-study, and the traveling name keep replacing resolved pressure with a larger one. | **9/10, high.** Each local payoff changes Cael's social position and creates the next problem without undercutting the win. |
