    30	
    31	"Good. Then it's not in your head any more. It's on the desk." He sat a while longer, a big quiet weight on the end of the bed, and Cael found that he did not mind the weight, and that the beams were easier to look at with it there. After a while Brom said, "You knock well now. Half, on a floor. That's more than I had at your age."
    32	
    33	"You're a year older than me."
    34	
