editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-35.md:5:He knew the hand: every letter on the front was the same height as its neighbour, level as a ruled line, the hand of a young man who had been told once that neatness was a kind of honesty and had believed it. Coss had read that hand on a routing card some weeks ago, on a short return from the river side, and had gone down to the long room at the end of the day to look at a file he had no reason to look at. He had not expected to see it again so soon. He had not expected to see it at all.
