editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-35.md:191:They went out at the side door into the cold. Lira was waiting under the lamp at the corner, with her coat buttoned to the chin and her staff on her shoulder, and she did not ask anything. She only looked at Cael's face, and took his arm on the side away from the lanes, and walked.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-35.md:203:On the way out he did the one other thing he could think of. He walked from the end of the back bench to the last lamp on the west wall, in his ordinary steps, and counted. Fourteen. In the alcove, the first week of the season, tired and not trying, he had had six. He wrote the two numbers one under the other on the inside of his wrist in pencil, so that he would see them every time he washed, and did not wash them off for a week.
