## (1) Brief items

### Priority 1 — Define and keep the consent boundary: RESOLVED

The repair replaces the absolute rule with a concrete distinction between ambient presence and a targeted read. Chapter 32's zero-context diff changes:

> pre-repair: `A thing I can do to people without their knowing is a thing I have to ask before I do.`
>
> current: `What a person gives off to a room belongs to the room: that they're there, where, still or moving, how they press. ... Going into one person on purpose, to find out what's in them ... belongs to them. That I ask before I do.`

Brom gives the same boundary in speech: `Mine lies on the room ... That's the room's. Going into somebody's another thing.` The rule is therefore understandable before later scenes test it.

Chapter 33 no longer lets Cael read three strangers and proceed as though nothing happened. The diff replaces the completed public test with an immediate recognition:

> `I just went into him. The old man. I didn't ask.`

> `And I set it you, and didn't think. ... That's mine, then, as much as yours.`

The remaining discrimination work is explicitly consensual: `They did the rest of it that week in the alcove, with people who had said yes.` Lira, the dock partner, the heavyset man, and the girl from Keth's ring each grant leave. The Log now says `with leave`, and the Carrying column records: `The old man at the dray. Did. Didn't ask. Stopped.`

Chapters 34–36 keep the boundary. The repaired sweep says `He did not go into anybody`; the first false reading is reduced from `kindled` to the room-level facts `somebody, low, still`; the market confirmation says `He did not go into it`; Brom states `not go into them, either; same rule as anybody`; the vigil is planned to `take nothing but what the room was given`; and its Log closes `Neither of us went in.` In the archive, Cael recognizes that ambient awareness of Vell would put him `a short step to going in`, notes that he has not asked, and closes the sense.

The repaired boundary is morally legible, operationally consistent, and carried through every later use.

### Priority 2.1 — Make the notebook-security answer complete: RESOLVED

The pre-repair condition—`a full name beside a fighter who was not in Vell's ledger`—is gone. The current text says:

